  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Agent Discord Presence",
      "text": "Discord Rich Presence for Codex, Claude Code, OpenCode, Pi, and DeepSeek Harness, powered by one local service that keeps your active work visible in Discord.\n\n> [!NOTE]\\\n> This project is in early development, so expect frequent changes."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- Generates a summary title, subtitle, activity state, and elapsed session time for your active agent work.\n- Selects the active session across supported agents, reconnects to Discord, and clears stale sessions automatically.\n- Uses the current agent model by default for summaries, with optional custom model, service, language, and prompt styling.\n- Sends up to 4,000 characters of the completed assistant reply to the summarization model and includes model usage metadata.\n- Allows automatic summaries to be disabled while keeping lifecycle updates enabled.\n- Runs multiple agents together with [independent model, prompt, and display settings](USAGE.md#independent-configuration-for-each-agent)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Quick start",
      "text": "The easiest way to get started is to let your agent handle the setup. Paste this repository link into your agent, or copy the prompt below:\n\n```text\nInstall and configure agent-discord-presence for the agent I'm using:\nhttps://github.com/LitoMore/agent-discord-presence\n\nRead the README and USAGE.md, check the prerequisites, install the package,"
    },
    {
      "section": "Quick start",
      "text": "You'll need Node.js 22+ and the Discord desktop app. Open Discord and sign in before checking your presence. A default Discord Application ID is included; no bot token is needed.\n\nPrefer to set it up yourself? Install the package and start the service in the background:\n\n```sh\nnpm install --global agent-discord-presence\nadp start -b\n```\n\nThen follow the setup instructions for your agent:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Quick start",
      "text": "- [Codex](USAGE.md#codex)\n- [Claude Code](USAGE.md#claude-code)\n- [OpenCode](USAGE.md#opencode)\n- [Pi](USAGE.md#pi)\n- [DeepSeek Harness](USAGE.md#deepseek-harness)\n\nOnce connected, give your agent a task and check Discord for its activity. Run `adp status` to check the service and Discord connection."
    },
    {
      "section": "Quick start",
      "text": "Stop the service with `adp stop`; this clears its Discord activity. To run in the foreground instead, use `adp start` and stop it with Ctrl+C. Automatic startup is not configured, so run `adp start -b` again after restarting your computer."
    },
    {
      "section": "Documentation",
      "text": "- [Images and display settings](USAGE.md#images-and-display-settings)\n- [Prompts and language](USAGE.md#default-presence-prompts)\n- [Model and service selection](USAGE.md#automatic-generation-and-model-selection)\n- [Presence layout and manual summaries](USAGE.md#summary-title-layout)\n- [Session selection and lifecycle](USAGE.md#session-selection-and-lifecycle)\n- [Configuration and platform notes](USAGE.md#configuration-and-platform-notes)"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
